    "case_summary": "A 43-year-old woman presented with abnormal vaginal bleeding. Family history was significant for prostate cancer in her father and paternal grandfather.\n\nNo physical examination findings were explicitly mentioned in the case report.\n\n{'Pathology Tests': {'Initial Test': 'Dilation and curettage was performed', 'Immunohistochemistry': 'Tumor stained negative for MSH6 protein', 'Microsatellite Instability (MSI) Testing': 'MSI testing was negative', 'Genetic Testing': 'Germline mutation R1331X was detected in the MSH6 gene'}}\n\nWhat is the most likely diagnosis?\n\nOptions:\nA. Sporadic endometrial carcinoma\nB. Lynch syndrome–associated endometrial carcinoma\nC. Stage IA endometrial cancer\nD. Endometrial carcinoma associated with Lynch syndrome\n",
